  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:4162",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that gefitinib interacts with the Fatty acid oxidation complex subunit alpha through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is directly linked to the ES1 protein, which in turn targets the fatty acid oxidation complex subunit alpha. Additionally, gefitinib is associated with Atypical kinase COQ8B, a protein that is targeted by flavopiridol, which also targets the same subunit. Furthermore, gefitinib is linked to TAO1, a kinase that is targeted by Theasaponin E1, which also targets the fatty acid oxidation complex subunit alpha. These findings collectively imply that gefitinib exerts its effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of the fatty acid oxidation complex. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential to influence metabolic processes by targeting key components of the fatty acid oxidation pathway.",
